From cc0cba0ddfb1195fbb088d7fdc1b5a9f44af0420 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:45:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ArtCraft: the name the user reads and its USB folder

Everything the user reads says ArtCraft instead of MihawkOS or Mihawk OS:
the PS5 tile's name (param.json titleName; its picture is the next
commit's, with the Start button's mark), the guided setup in its nine
languages, the launcher's pages, the loading screen, the desktop shortcuts'
tips, the detailed logs' README, the browser's window title, the install package's README, the
runtime wallpaper's corner note (now only the name). The library's own
desktop entry is "ArtCraft Windows desktop".

The USB stick's folder of runtime pieces is artcraft/, as the setup now
tells the user; the installer still takes a mihawkos/ folder from a stick
made for MihawkOS. The pack format's own tags (mihawkos-runtime-pack and
the like) are not names the user reads and stay, as the packs carry them.

The credits stay Mihawk's: About says ArtCraft is "a modified version of
MihawkOS. Copyright (C) 2026 Mihawk and the authors credited in NOTICE.md"
(GPLv3 section 5a) and names both source repositories; the music is
"Original music by Mihawk". Identifiers nobody reads stay so tools, formats
and prefixes keep working: window classes, HKCU\Software\Mihawk keys, the
mihawk prefix id, mihawk.exe, MihawkBrowser.lnk.

The title tags its log with its name, so lines read [ArtCraft]: the console
tools (run-console.py, run-launcher.py, run-setup-unattended.py) and their
tests look for that tag.

Made by PS5-ARTCRAFT's artcraft_ps5/rebrand.py, whose every rule must match
as often as it says (a new Mihawk OS that moved a string stops it).

Proven on the host: tests/test_pw_setup.c (9 of 9 languages with complete
drawable text: every glyph of the new name is in the baked font),
tests/test_pw_detailed_logs.c (ASan, UBSan), tests/test_package_install.py;
ps5/src/proton_launch.cpp and proton_install.cpp compile in the
host-reference configuration. tests/test_console_setup.py,
test_run_console_verdicts.py and test_console_guard.py need ../PS5_Vulkan's
ps5_console and were not run; their change is the tag alone, made the same
in the tools they test. No console run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ErqzkhbC5fRkeGcCmR5R95
